Maybe I'm not understanding the design appropriately but this doesn't seem like a less-than-perfect detection/occupancy problem for which occu addresses.  If the cage of mussels is placed in the river, then it would seem that the whole downstream is by definition "occupied" and it's only an issue of less-than-perfect detection that almost certainly decreases as one goes downstream.  As such it would seem that a logistic regression would be appropriate.

Also, such an analysis would refer to this particular stream (and its structure of pools, riffles, and runs).  With respect to making a general inference to all streams this is a sample of size 1.

Others should certainly weigh in on this.

Jim

